# [[.Label]]

This directory contains editable Schema DSL declarations in `modeldef/schema.go`.
App creation has not installed the app, changed generated models, or opened a
database. The directory can be kept in a project or packaged for reuse.

## Register in a project

For a project created by `godj startproject`, edit its `modeldef/apps.go`:

1. Import this directory's `modeldef` package with an explicit alias such as
   `newappdef`. For `example.com/my-site/apps/[[.Label]]`, the import is
   `newappdef "example.com/my-site/apps/[[.Label]]/modeldef"`.
2. Add `newappdef.Definition()` to the returned `[]schema.Definition`, keeping
   the existing app definitions.
3. Run `godj generate`, `godj makemigrations`, review the migration, then run
   `godj migrate`. Restart the server to use the new app.

An empty app has an identity and no tables. Add models to `Definition()` using
the public Schema DSL. The starter project places generated models at
`apps/[[.Label]]/models`; keep declarations separate from those output files.
Other project layouts can include the definition through their own `ProjectSpec`
and choose explicit package aliases and output locations.

Choose exposed fields and permissions when registering Admin resources or API
routes. Creating or installing an app does not expose its models automatically.
An app label must be unique among the project's installed definitions. Schema
and generator validation reject duplicates before publishing a new bundle.
